speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, there have been discussions on both sides of the House, and I believe you will find that there is consent for the following motion:
That, immediately following the adoption of this motion, these provisions be in force for proceedings in the House this day, notwithstanding any Standing Order:
1.	Supplementary Estimates (B) be tabled and referred to various Standing Committees as in the motion of the President of the Treasury Board, without question being put;
2.	Orders of the Day be called immediately thereafter, until Statements by Members at 11 o'clock a.m., followed by Oral Questions at 11.15 o'clock a.m.;
3.	All Routine Proceedings be called at noon in the usual manner, followed by Government Orders until 2 o'clock p.m., during which time
a)	Bill C-92, an act to amend the Northwest Territories Act, shall be disposed of at all stages, on division, and
b)	Government Business No. 23 respecting the appointment of a Special Committee to study the subject-matter of Bill C-80, an act to amend the Criminal Code and the Customs Tariff in consequence thereof, and any amendments thereto, shall be disposed of on division;
4.	Private Members' Business be called at the usual time;
5.	At the completion of the time provided for consideration of Private Members' Business the House suspend to the call of the Chair, for the sole purpose of receiving a message respecting the giving of Royal Assent to Bill C-87, an act to amend the statue law in relation to war veterans, later this day, and that following such Royal Assent, upon return to this Chamber, the Speaker shall adjourn the House until 1 o'clock p.m. Monday, November 26, 1990.
